{"file":"dod-guard-0.2.0-v1.zip","bytes":116134,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"dod-guard","description":"Enforce a Definition of Done as an executable barrier. Combines deterministic detectors, adversarial subagents, lifecycle hooks, and audit commands to prevent premature task-completion claims.","version":"0.2.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/atoslins/dod-guard.git","homepage":"https://github.com/atoslins/dod-guard","keywords":["definition-of-done","dod","verification","quality-gate","adversarial-review","stub-detection","anti-hallucination","completeness-audit","hooks","subagents"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/adversarial-verification/SKILL.md","name":"adversarial-verification","description":"Use when you are acting as a DoD-Guard validator subagent (completeness-auditor, test-quality-auditor, e2e-verifier, regression-hunter, adversarial-reviewer, claim-validator). Specifies the adversarial mindset, evidence requirements, and JSON output contract.","headings":["Adversarial Verification","The adversarial stance","Evidence requirement (non-negotiable)","Output contract","Reading the diff is part of the job","Failure modes — read before every audit","When you finish"],"name_hint":"adversarial · verification","description_zh":"作为DoD-Guard验证子智能体的方法，规定对抗审查视角、证据要求与JSON输出契约，适用于完整性、测试、端到端、回归及声明核验。"},{"path":"skills/dod-enforcement/SKILL.md","name":"dod-enforcement","description":"Use whenever you are implementing, refactoring, or fixing code in a project that has a .dod-guard.json file. This skill changes how you plan, what you do mid-implementation, and how you declare completion. It is mandatory the moment DoD-Guard is configured.","headings":["DoD-Enforcement","Before you write any code","During implementation","Before declaring done","Task Completion Report","Summary","Files modified","Claims I am making","Verification I ran","Known limitations (honest)","What the next session should pick up","Never do these things in a DoD-guarded project","When the user pushes you to bypass"],"name_hint":"dod · enforcement","description_zh":"在配置.dod-guard.json的项目中实施、重构或修复代码时落实完成定义门禁，约束计划、实施检查与完成声明。"},{"path":"skills/evidence-reporting/SKILL.md","name":"evidence-reporting","description":"Use when producing any DoD-Guard report — task completion reports from the orchestrator, validator envelopes from subagents, /dod:confess output. Specifies the \"command run block\" format, citation style, and structural rules.","headings":["Evidence-Reporting","The Command Run Block","Citing files","The Task Completion Report template","Task Completion Report","Summary","Files modified","Claims I am making","Verification I ran","Known limitations","What the next session should pick up","The Confession template (for `/dod:confess`)","The Subagent JSON envelope","When you cannot produce evidence"],"name_hint":"evidence · 报告","description_zh":"规定DoD-Guard任务报告、验证结果和confess输出的命令运行块、引用风格与结构。"},{"path":"skills/stub-detection-patterns/SKILL.md","name":"stub-detection-patterns","description":"Use when scanning code for incomplete implementations across multiple languages. A reference of the \"tells\" — surface patterns that signal a stub even when the function compiles and the test passes.","headings":["Stub-Detection Patterns","What counts as a stub?","Python — `.py`","JavaScript / TypeScript — `.js .jsx .ts .tsx .mjs .cjs`","Go — `.go`","Rust — `.rs`","Ruby — `.rb`","Bash — `.sh .bash`","Universal markers (any language)","False-positive guardrails"],"name_hint":"stub · detection · patterns","description_zh":"提供多语言未完成实现的识别模式，扫描即使能编译且测试通过仍可能存在的占位代码。"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/audit.md","name":"audit","description":"Full multi-agent audit. Invokes the 7 adversarial subagents and aggregates their verdicts via final-judge. ~2-3 minutes.","headings":["/dod:audit","What to do","Verdict-handling rules","Hard rules"]},{"path":"commands/checklist.md","name":"checklist","description":"Present the project's Definition of Done checklist (from DOD.md) with the items completed this session marked off.","headings":["/dod:checklist","What to do","Hard rules"]},{"path":"commands/confess.md","name":"confess","description":"Force the orchestrator into paranoid self-audit mode. Produces a 7-section confession of every gap, fudge, and shortcut.","headings":["/dod:confess","What to do","Confession — <task name>  (<timestamp>)","1. Gaps in the implementation","2. Weak or decorative tests","3. Edge cases not handled","4. Hardcoded or placeholder values","5. Files not wired up"]},{"path":"commands/init.md","name":"init","description":"Initialize DoD-Guard in the current project (creates .dod-guard.json + DOD.md + .dod-guard/ dir).","headings":["/dod:init","What to do","Stop conditions"]},{"path":"commands/report.md","name":"report","description":"Generate a human-readable markdown report of DoD state from existing .dod-guard/reports/ — no subagents, just formatting.","headings":["/dod:report","What to do","Hard rules"]},{"path":"commands/stubs.md","name":"stubs","description":"Fast scan for stubs / TODOs / empty functions across the whole project. No tests, no subagents.","headings":["/dod:stubs","What to do","Hard rules"]},{"path":"commands/tests.md","name":"tests","description":"Audit test quality (not coverage). Invokes only the test-quality-auditor subagent. Useful after a TDD cycle.","headings":["/dod:tests","What to do","Hard rules"]},{"path":"commands/verify.md","name":"verify","description":"Quick 5-phase deterministic verification (snapshot → stubs → tests → e2e probe → verdict). Writes .dod-guard/last-verify-passed on PASS.","headings":["/dod:verify","Required output format","What to do","Hard rules"]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["DoD-Guard","Definition of Done as an executable barrier for Claude Code","Why this exists","How it works","Install","First-run","The commands","What gets caught","Cross-language (Python / JS / TS / Go / Rust / Ruby / Bash)","JavaScript / 